// CACHE: GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/commits | owner=CodeEditorLand | repo=Cocoon | per_page=5 | page=59 → GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/commits.RESPONSE.map(Author,Date,File,Message,SHA)
{
	"Set": [
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T04:14:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				274,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Implement message dialog item selection and real document loading\n\nEnhance Window service message dialogs (showInformationMessage, showWarningMessage, showErrorMessage) to properly handle the items parameter by sending gRPC requests with items to Mountain and returning the selected item from the response.\n\nEnhance Workspace service openTextDocument to fetch actual file content from Mountain via fs.readFile instead of returning mock data. Implement full TextDocument interface with proper getText(range), lineAt, offsetAt, positionAt, validateRange, validatePosition methods. Add language detection based on file extension mapping.\n\nAlso add workspace folder DTO conversion to VSCode.WorkspaceFolder objects in AcceptWorkspaceData handler. Remove stale TODO comments about event stream emitters and WorkspaceConfiguration that have been addressed.\n\nThese changes complete the basic document opening flow, enabling real file content to be displayed in the editor with proper language detection.",
			"SHA": "9d2577507d57c5a63c5252240ddabb24c0e3e747"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T04:08:29Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				274,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Implement webview IPC notifications to Mountain\n\nReplace TODO placeholder implementations in WindowService's IPC proxy with actual gRPC notifications to Mountain backend. SendNotification now posts messages to the webview panel via webview.postMessage, SendRequest returns undefined as it's fire-and-forget (Sky resolves via onDidReceiveMessage), and the dispose callback notifies Mountain to destroy the webview panel via webview.dispose.\n\nThis completes the webview lifecycle IPC integration, enabling Cocoon to properly communicate panel state changes to Mountain.",
			"SHA": "7461ad28e3ff0c40a92feb6556104465e6503f6e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T04:06:53Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				274,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Implement progress IPC notifications to Mountain\n\nReplace TODO placeholder implementations in the WithProgress API with actual gRPC notifications to Mountain backend. The report() method now sends progress.update notifications, progress start sends progress.start with location/title/cancellable options, and progress complete sends progress.complete.\n\nThis enables the Mountain backend to display real-time progress indicators while VS Code extensions execute long-running tasks.\n\nAlso fixes shell script shebangs from bash to sh for broader POSIX compatibility.",
			"SHA": "0518541ec93665ca1456d290e8ffa02abea4dccf"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T03:39:01Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				274,
				18
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Implement Mountain IPC calls in WindowService\n\nReplace TODO placeholder implementations in WindowService with actual gRPC notifications to Mountain. Status bar items now send setStatusBarText, setStatusBarTooltip, disposeStatusBarItem notifications. Output channels implement full IPC: output.create, output.append, output.appendLine, output.clear, output.show, output.dispose.\n\nAlso includes code formatting improvements across services (APIFactory, APIFactoryService, FileSystemService, Workspace) and documentation cleanup removing resolved items from TODO tracking. ESBuild configs reformatted from minified to readable.\n\nThis completes the Window service integration layer, enabling the editor UI to properly communicate with Mountain backend.",
			"SHA": "a7f0e2ef5f9aa0dc3333dda5be07327596d545a3"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T03:16:41Z",
